{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "OnehotClipped",
  "description": "Structure-only merging (spec \u00a72.1). c: a level search kap = min{k : c[k] > 0.3} read as a subscript under a row-index ifelse, c[kap] on rows i <= 2 and c[6 - kap] on rows 3..5, so static clipping splits the one-hot column into two adjacent regions whose one-hot selections differ: full bands kept apart by their coefficients, one structure-only band. e: one state defined by two equations (rows 1..2, then 3..5) whose bands on c have the same structure and adjacent rows: never merged across the equations, in either mode."
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "x": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 5
  }
 },
